{"message": [{"role": "user", "content": "다음 코드를 리뷰해줘:\n\n```\n@@ -153,10 +162,16 @@ class AgentExecutor(Chain, BaseModel):\n \n```"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "It does get passed in to the child `LLMChain` but not the `LLMChain`'s `LLM`:\r\n\r\n```\r\n    manager = CallbackManager([handler])\r\n    tool = \"Search\"\r\n    responses = [\r\n        f\"FooBarBaz\\nAction: {tool}\\nAction Input: misalignment\",\r\n        \"Oh well\\nAction: Final Answer\\nAction Input: curses foiled again\",\r\n    ]\r\n    fake_llm = FakeListLLM(responses=responses, callback_manager=manager, verbose=True)\r\n    tools = [\r\n        Tool(\"Search\", lambda x: x, \"Useful for searching\"),\r\n    ]\r\n    agent = initialize_agent(\r\n        tools,\r\n        fake_llm,\r\n        agent=\"zero-shot-react-description\",\r\n        verbose=True,\r\n        callback_manager=manager,\r\n    )\r\n```\r\n\r\n^ this is the pattern you'd have to follow to get the callback manager to all children modules of the `AgentExecutor` (pass in `CallbackManager` to `LLM`) essentially.\r\n\r\nsee here for more details: https://github.com/hwchase17/langchain/blob/db5c8e0c42d9c38ea1373f1c0355698527350e61/langchain/agents/agent.py#L135"}]}
