{"message": [{"role": "user", "content": "다음 코드를 리뷰해줘:\n\n```\n@@ -153,10 +162,16 @@ class AgentExecutor(Chain, BaseModel):\n \n```"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Yes that pattern works fine when initialising, it's just annoying when you have to change the callback manager across the board for an existing agent that you don't want to throw away (because eg you want to keep memory)\r\n\r\nie. something like this\r\n\r\n```py\r\nclass MyLangchainAgent:\r\n    agent_executor: AgentExecutor\r\n    other_langchain_objects: list[Chain | BaseLLM] = []\r\n\r\n    def __init__(self, state: dict, loop: asyncio.AbstractEventLoop):\r\n        super().__init__(state, loop)\r\n\r\n        llm = OpenAI(temperature=0, verbose=True)\r\n        llm_math_chain = LLMMathChain(llm=llm, verbose=True)\r\n        tools = [\r\n            Tool(\r\n                name=\"Calculator\",\r\n                func=llm_math_chain.run,\r\n                description=\"useful for when you need to answer questions about math\",\r\n            ),\r\n        ]\r\n        self.agent_executor = initialize_agent(\r\n            tools, llm, agent=\"zero-shot-react-description\", verbose=True\r\n        )\r\n        self.langchain_objects = [llm_math_chain]\r\n\r\n    async def __call__(self, user_message: dict, ctx: RunContext):\r\n        # Set up callback manager for the run\r\n        callback_manager = CallbackManager([ConcatCallbackHandler(ctx)])\r\n        for obj in self.other_langchain_objects + [\r\n            self.agent_executor,\r\n            self.agent_executor.agent.llm_chain,\r\n            self.agent_executor.agent.llm_chain.llm,\r\n        ]:\r\n            obj.callback_manager = callback_manager\r\n\r\n        # Run the agent\r\n        await asyncio.get_event_loop().run_in_executor(\r\n            None, self.agent_executor.run, \"\".join(user_message[\"content_parts\"])\r\n        )\r\n```"}]}
