{"message": [{"role": "user", "content": "다음 코드를 리뷰해줘:\n\n```\n@@ -410,8 +404,8 @@ deprecated ``flaskext.foo``.  Flask 0.8 introduces a redirect import\n system that lets uses import from ``flask.ext.foo`` and it will try\n ``flask_foo`` first and if that fails ``flaskext.foo``.\n \n-Flask extensions should urge users to import from ``flask.ext.foo``\n-instead of ``flask_foo`` or ``flaskext_foo`` so that extensions can\n+Flask extensions should urge users to import from ``flask_foo``\n+instead of ``flask.ext.foo`` or ``flaskext_foo`` so that extensions can\n```"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "- flaskext.foo is the old thing\n- flask_foo is the new thing\n- flask.ext.foo is a \"fake package\" provided by Flask itself so app authors can import their extensions without having to worry which style the extension uses (whether it installs itself as flaskext.foo or flask_foo)\n- Nowadays flaskext.foo is not used anymore, so the compat package flask.ext.foo is not needed anymore, everybody should use flask_foo."}]}
