{"message": [{"role": "user", "content": "다음 코드를 리뷰해줘:\n\n```\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+Subclassing Flask\n+=================\n+\n+The :class:`~flask.Flask` class is designed for subclassing.\n+\n+One reason to subclass would be customizing the Jinja2 :class:`~jinja2.Environment`. For example, to add a new global template variable::\n+\n+    from flask import Flask\n+    from datetime import datetime\n+\n+    class MyFlask(Flask):\n+        \"\"\" Flask with more global template vars \"\"\"\n```"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "There shouldn't be surrounding whitespace"}]}
{"message": [{"role": "user", "content": "다음 코드를 리뷰해줘:\n\n```\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+Subclassing Flask\n+=================\n+\n+The :class:`~flask.Flask` class is designed for subclassing.\n+\n+One reason to subclass would be customizing the Jinja2 :class:`~jinja2.Environment`. For example, to add a new global template variable::\n+\n+    from flask import Flask\n+    from datetime import datetime\n+\n+    class MyFlask(Flask):\n+        \"\"\" Flask with more global template vars \"\"\"\n+\n+        def create_jinja_environment(self):\n+            \"\"\" Initialize my custom Jinja environment. \"\"\"\n+            jinja_env = super(MyFlask, self).create_jinja_environment(self)\n+            jinja_env.globals.update(\n+                current_time = datetime.datetime.now()\n```"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "kwargs don't have space around the `=` and this example doesn't seem particularly useful; especially considering that this probably runs once at setup time and there are already proper APIs in Flask to add new template globals, filters or tests without subclassing."}]}
{"message": [{"role": "user", "content": "다음 코드를 리뷰해줘:\n\n```\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+Subclassing Flask\n+=================\n+\n+The :class:`~flask.Flask` class is designed for subclassing.\n+\n+One reason to subclass would be customizing the Jinja2 :class:`~jinja2.Environment`. For example, to add a new global template variable::\n+\n+    from flask import Flask\n+    from datetime import datetime\n+\n+    class MyFlask(Flask):\n+        \"\"\" Flask with more global template vars \"\"\"\n+\n+        def create_jinja_environment(self):\n+            \"\"\" Initialize my custom Jinja environment. \"\"\"\n+            jinja_env = super(MyFlask, self).create_jinja_environment(self)\n+            jinja_env.globals.update(\n+                current_time = datetime.datetime.now()\n```"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Thanks for the quick feedback. Any suggestions for a better subclassing use-case?"}]}
{"message": [{"role": "user", "content": "다음 코드를 리뷰해줘:\n\n```\n@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@\n+Subclassing Flask\n+=================\n+\n+The :class:`~flask.Flask` class is designed for subclassing.\n+\n+One reason to subclass would be customizing the Jinja2 :class:`~jinja2.Environment`. For example, to add a new global template variable::\n+\n+    from flask import Flask\n+    from datetime import datetime\n+\n+    class MyFlask(Flask):\n+        \"\"\" Flask with more global template vars \"\"\"\n+\n+        def create_jinja_environment(self):\n+            \"\"\" Initialize my custom Jinja environment. \"\"\"\n+            jinja_env = super(MyFlask, self).create_jinja_environment(self)\n+            jinja_env.globals.update(\n+                current_time = datetime.datetime.now()\n```"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'm not sure if there is any good reason to override this specific method."}]}
