{"message": [{"role": "user", "content": "다음 코드를 리뷰해줘:\n\n```\n@@ -171,6 +171,30 @@ def is_scalar_sequence_field(field: Field) -> bool:\n     return False\n \n \n+def get_typed_signature(call: Callable) -> inspect.Signature:\n```"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I originally wanted to use `typing.get_type_hints` directly, but ultimately this implementation seemed cleaner and follows `typing.get_type_hints` where it matters (namely, using the same logic to determine the local and global namespaces, and essentially using the same logic to evaluate string references by converting them to forward references (and evaluating those forward references).\r\n\r\nIt also uses `pydantic.utils` to handle differences between the `typing` api for python 3.6 and 3.7 (for `ForwardRef` and `evaluate_forwardref` anyway), and to deal with the fact that the relevant objects are technically private in `typing`. Since `pydantic` has made them public, it seems reasonable to let `pydantic` worry about ensuring the public API is stable. Moreover, this ensures compatibility with the way pydantic handles forward references anyway."}]}
