{"message": [{"role": "user", "content": "다음 코드를 리뷰해줘:\n\n```\n@@ -253,17 +253,16 @@ def __init__(\n         name: str = None,\n         dependency_overrides_provider: Any = None,\n     ) -> None:\n-        self.path = path\n-        self.endpoint = endpoint\n-        self.name = get_name(endpoint) if name is None else name\n+        super().__init__(\n+            path=path, endpoint=endpoint, name=name,\n+        )\n```"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "There we can get overhead since both `WebSocketRoute` and `APIWebSocketRoute` will call `websocket_session`.\r\nCurrently it only makes coroutine, so nothing bad happens"}]}
{"message": [{"role": "user", "content": "다음 코드를 리뷰해줘:\n\n```\n@@ -253,17 +253,16 @@ def __init__(\n         name: str = None,\n         dependency_overrides_provider: Any = None,\n     ) -> None:\n-        self.path = path\n-        self.endpoint = endpoint\n-        self.name = get_name(endpoint) if name is None else name\n+        super().__init__(\n+            path=path, endpoint=endpoint, name=name,\n```"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Case, when `name` argument is None, has already covered at the base class and it used the same `get_name ` function.\r\n\r\nThis is a code of a part of a `starllet.routing.WebSocketRoute` class:\r\n```python\r\nclass WebSocketRoute(BaseRoute):\r\n    def __init__(\r\n        self, path: str, endpoint: typing.Callable, *, name: str = None\r\n    ) -> None:\r\n        assert path.startswith(\"/\"), \"Routed paths must start with '/'\"\r\n        self.path = path\r\n        self.endpoint = endpoint\r\n        self.name = get_name(endpoint) if name is None else name\r\n\r\n        if inspect.isfunction(endpoint) or inspect.ismethod(endpoint):\r\n            # Endpoint is function or method. Treat it as `func(websocket)`.\r\n            self.app = websocket_session(endpoint)\r\n        else:\r\n            # Endpoint is a class. Treat it as ASGI.\r\n            self.app = endpoint\r\n\r\n        self.path_regex, self.path_format, self.param_convertors = compile_path(path)\r\n```"}]}
